  "slug": "artist:akale-wube",
  "name": "Akalé Wubé",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in Paris in 2009, the French quintet Akalé Wubé built their output on a modern reinterpretation of 1960s Ethiopian jazz and funk. Their name, meaning \"beauty of the soul\" in Amharique, defined a decade of international touring across Europe, China, and Africa. The group achieved significant acclaim for their contribution to the Buda Musique label's \"Éthiopiques\" series with the 2017 album \"Mistakes on Purpose,\" which featured the veteran Ethiopian musician Girma Bèyènè. Throughout their career, they collaborated with luminaries such as Manu Dibango and Mahmoud Ahmed. Their instrumental arrangements frequently utilized the krar, mbira, and brass sections to honor the traditions established by artists like Mulatu Astatke. The group disbanded in April 2021 after twelve years of recording and live performance.",
